{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191215-nameless-war-\u2013-fan-approach","id":1191215,"title":"Nameless War \u2013 Fan Approach","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-02T20:00:37-08:00","id":1191215,"title":"Nameless War \u2013 Fan Approach","content":"As we are years before <b>Tome of Pentacle</b> to spot some official light on Nameless War events in <b>Mage \u2013 </b>let\u2019s talk about it, in fans takes. Here is my interpretation of events - it's more guessing but based on 1E and 2E gameline materials. Strong inspiration for this I had from <i>Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrell</i> ( book or TV series ) and <i>Hamilton</i> ( rap musical about Founding Fathers of America ).<br /> <br /> <b>Notice:</b> <b>We talk here about Nameless Movement, <i>not</i> faction or Order.</b> We treat all the Nameless as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Social_movement\" target=\"_blank\">Social Movement</a> - with first groups like Pirate Republic of Nassau - that comes and goes until year 1900, when most of this Movement become Free Council. Prior to this, Nameless Movement is coalition of various groups and cults, sometimes fighting one another AND Diamond and Seers - similar to the later Civil Rights, LGBT+ and Environmental Movements. Basically Nameless War is one century of inter- and outer- Nameless Movements conflicts for fresh Nameless.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Circa 1765 - Sleepers start their American Revolution ideas</b> \u2013 with famous 'No Taxation Without Representation' idea. Revolution starts as movement.</li> <li><b>Since 1765 - Rise of Adamantine Arrow in Diamond Orders at large</b> - it's the preparation for the <i>War</i> of Independence, in the end. Many young mages are preparing for fighting and join Arrow to be prepared, sensing coming conflict.</li> <li><b>Circa 1770 - Starts of proper American War of Independence</b> \u2013 American \u2013 Britain tension rise to highest with Boston Massacre in 1770. Armed incidents are spreading in Colonise. Seers connected with British Empire are attacking Diamond in battle.</li> <li><b>1770 - Destruction of transcontinental relations between Diamond and Seers Orders members with start of War for </b><b>Independence.</b> So New York Silver Ladder caucus stops to answer to the 'higher-ups' in London \u2013 and alike.</li> <li><b>Since 1770 - Rise of Nameless mages in numbers on general, from the chaos of War of Independence in Sleepers society. </b>Weaken Diamond as organisation means more freshly Awakened are not recruited by using Labirynth, Cryptopoly or other typical mechanism. Those left alone new mages are more prone to rebel to authority of Orders in general - and so risen in times of Sleepers revolution - have strong antiauthoritarian views, building proper Nameless Movement and passing Revolution from Sleepers to Awakened society at dawn of 19th century, with information about French Revolution.</li> <li><b>1785 \u2013 1793(?) Creation of Nameless Movement.</b> At the start, Nameless were group of Nameless Cults (Orders) groups fighting with Diamond, Seers or even themselves \u2013 after seeing that American and French Revolutions come to fruition. It's more accurate to talk about Nameless Movement than Nameless (global) Order, as each faction wanted to pull and win <i>their</i> side of narrative.</li> <li><b>Till 1793(?) - Post Sleepers American and French Revolutions</b>, <b>till start of proper Nameless War -</b> Newly recruited in Revolution and not fully formed young Adamantine Arrows are 'bored' in peaceful live of Awakened now, when all they know is battle magic. When Nameless Movement start to take shape, many of those young Arrows are joining various Nameless factions, just to have excuse to fight with their old Orders siblings and in spite of their previous mentors.</li> <li><b>1793 - War of Nameless has started in Awakened society</b>, when Sleepers Revolutions are slowly ending. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign_of_Terror\" target=\"_blank\">Reign of Terror</a> in France push parts of Hegemonic Ministry to go into coalition with local Nameless Movement factions - and Nameless respond with violence, starting Nameless War.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-04-2018, 05:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T21:52:18-08:00","id":1191245,"title":"","content":"I'd leave out the US revolution in my reckoning, because it wasn't really a revolution. It was a British civil war over who got to control the future of colonial expansion in North America. I'd associate the Seers with the slaveowners of Virginia, such as Jefferson and Washington. That said, the propaganda promoting the American revolution would likely backfire on the Seers, inspiring revolutions in Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T05:40:11-08:00","id":1191317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191215-nameless-war-\u2013-fan-approach?p=1191245#post1191245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd leave out the US revolution in my reckoning, because it wasn't really a revolution. It was a British civil war over who got to control the future of colonial expansion in North America. I'd associate the Seers with the slaveowners of Virginia, such as Jefferson and Washington. That said, the propaganda promoting the American revolution would likely backfire on the Seers, inspiring revolutions in Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, still, American War of Independence would heighten the numbers of future Nameless - starting Nameless Movement just by numbers risen in phenomena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T13:02:06-08:00","id":1191425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191215-nameless-war-\u2013-fan-approach?p=1191317#post1191317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, still, American War of Independence would heighten the numbers of future Nameless - starting Nameless Movement just by numbers risen in phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another early revolution that I think would have a stronger effect on the formation of the Nameless would be the Haitian revolution. There you have real revolution throwing off the yoke of slavery, tyranny, and exploitation. Of course, that revolution was opposed by Washington and the new American government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T13:47:27-08:00","id":1191440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191215-nameless-war-\u2013-fan-approach?p=1191425#post1191425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another early revolution that I think would have a stronger effect on the formation of the Nameless would be the Haitian revolution. There you have real revolution throwing off the yoke of slavery, tyranny, and exploitation. Of course, that revolution was opposed by Washington and the new American government.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively if you want an earlier revolution that is thematically resonant with the Nameless trying to throw of the yoke of the Orders, maybe look at the English Civil War and Cromwellian England.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T20:13:06-08:00","id":1191513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191215-nameless-war-\u2013-fan-approach?p=1191425#post1191425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another early revolution that I think would have a stronger effect on the formation of the Nameless would be the Haitian revolution. There you have real revolution throwing off the yoke of slavery, tyranny, and exploitation. Of course, that revolution was opposed by Washington and the new American government.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating - I did know that Revolution on Haiti took place, but did not know it was so radical, in the Franks &quot;Liberty, Equality, Fraternity&quot; kind of way. And Washington's answer to it really points that it was more in a way 'we left the things they were before - only we are now in power'. Yeah, thanks for pointing me to the hypocrytical stench of American Revolution ( that we, in reverse, have in Poland now ).<br /> <br /> <b>So yes, it sounds that American Revolution would be more about change of higher-ups in Diamond than proper formation of Nameless Movement - Nameless phenomena would just be 'collator damage' to Awakened society, coming from Americans-British de facto Civil War and many new Awakened not having proper training.</b> It's just that ideas start to spread and when Revolution comes to France and Haiti - it's much more egalitarian from the start. So the Nameless Movement being the thing already - Seers inside Jacobians comes to ask if they do not join them. And then we have official start of Nameless War...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-03-2018, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T20:24:55-08:00","id":1191516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191215-nameless-war-\u2013-fan-approach?p=1191440#post1191440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively if you want an earlier revolution that is thematically resonant with the Nameless trying to throw of the yoke of the Orders, maybe look at the English Civil War and Cromwellian England.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, did not wanting to go as much against the books - wanted just to see on what dates proper Nameless War could start. But if I remember correctly <b>Shadows of U.K. </b>book, Cromwellian England is even pointed as foundation for British Free Council - so it works exactly as previous seed of Nameless Movement that simply do not take whole world in it and was quickly deminished by imperialist Diamond and Seers Orders. It even make sense that then this Silver Ladder - Seers alliance would want to squash another 'fire' of Nameless Movement take on Awakened - i.e. Pirate Republic of Nassau! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>It really now has sense! Nameless War started only because Nameless Movement at the end of 18th century finally took world spanning - starting maybe in America, but then sweeping with France and Haiti - and then spread around the world. What we call Nameless now (as ideology) existed before - they just were too small force to be real threat to Diamond and Seers Orders before.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T02:32:17-08:00","id":1191582,"title":"","content":"I added to opening post clariefiction for what meant Nameless Movement and where Nameless War properly started.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1191215-nameless-war-\u2013-fan-approach#post1191215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Till 1793(?) - Post Sleepers American and French Revolutions</b>, <b>till start of proper Nameless War -</b> Newly recruited in Revolution and not fully formed young Adamantine Arrows are 'bored' in peaceful live of Awakened now, when all they know is battle magic. When Nameless Movement start to take shape, many of those young Arrows are joining various Nameless factions, just to have excuse to fight with their old Orders siblings and in spite of their previous mentors.</li> <li><b>1793 - War of Nameless has started in Awakened society</b>, when Sleepers Revolutions are slowly ending. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reign_of_Terror\" target=\"_blank\">Reign of Terror</a> in France push parts of Hegemonic Ministry to go into coalition with local Nameless Movement factions - and Nameless respond with violence, starting Nameless War.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:54:54-08:00","id":1191647,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for inspiration, I'd suggest reading up on the history of communism as an example of what is probably the most successful global movement. Not just in terms of violent revolutions everywhere, but where the leaders of those revolutions came from, where they got their ideas (not just the ideological ones, but the strategic ones), where they traveled to and who they talked with. You don't have to agree with communism to track the methodologies they used to spread their belief.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, I'd also suggest looking at the Non-Aligned Movement, which began during the Cold War as a kind of third option between the two major superpower blocs. They self-described as &quot;history's biggest peace-movement&quot; and can give some color to what motivations for Nameless organizational efforts may have been working towards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T14:45:45-07:00","id":1194635,"title":"","content":"Being today in small Internet conflict with Polish LGBT Catholics organisation over LGBT issues - I finally think I get how Nameless feel inside their own Movement. Every faction was having it's own philosophy, only meshing in Nameless War because they were all were shunned by majority of Awakened society - i.e. Diamond and Seers. And, hell, they discussion and philosophical differences could be <b><i>heated </i></b>inside Nameless!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T17:41:59-07:00","id":1339088,"title":"","content":"If your history of the nameless war doesn't have Pontiac's War, the Haitian Revolution, and the masonic conflicts in pre-independence Mexico City as more contributive, I'm not sure. I understand that the canonical books reference it as a defining moment, but I'd honestly really object to the idea that the slave owner/land speculator counterrevolution of 1776 has much to tell mages who eventually violently oppose the Seers. Now, if you posit the counterrevolution of 1776 as a seizure of state and power by Seers and possibly allied Diamond order mages I think you might get more traction to be historic.<br /> <br /> That said, it's likely that there were precursors to the coming nameless war in the pre-1776 colonial conflicts in North America, Africa, and Asia. You could also put precedent on the Glorious Revolution in England (see A Field in England).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25371,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25371-elzopilote","user":"elzopilote","date":". 10-02-2019, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25371-elzopilote","name":"elzopilote","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25371_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}